cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DescriptorPin, please cite it as below."
title: "DescriptorPin: a defensive integrity monitor for MCP tool descriptors"
abstract: >-
  DescriptorPin pins a canonical hash of every Model Context Protocol tool
  descriptor and reports silent mutation, cross-server name collisions,
  instruction-shaped description text, and stdio transport risk on a later
  scan. It detects and describes structural shapes; it does not claim to
  detect malice.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "the DescriptorPin authors"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - mcp
  - security
  - tool-poisoning
  - integrity
  - descriptor
repository-code: "[REPOSITORY URL]"

